'''''Brachythecium salebrosum''''' is a species of [[moss]] in the [[Brachytheciaceae]] family.<ref name="GBIF">{{GBIF |id=8418702|taxon=''Brachythecium salebrosum'' |accessdate=22 October 2022}}</ref> It is widely distributed throughout the world, except for in South-America and in tropical regions.<ref name="GBIF"/>

''Brachythecium salebrosum'' is known to be able to use [[artificial light]] to grow in places which are otherwise devoid of natural light, such as [[Crystal Cave (Wisconsin)|Crystal Cave]] in [[Wisconsin]].<ref name="Thatcher 1949">{{cite journal |last1=Thatcher |first1=Edward P. |title=Bryophytes of an Artificially Illuminated Cave |journal=The Bryologist |date=1949 |volume=52 |issue=4 |pages=212–214 |doi=10.2307/3239480 }}</ref>

